From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei Radulescu <andi.radulescu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 16:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] power: reset: msm: restart into EDL through PS_HOLD

The SCM driver programs emergency download mode for "reboot edl", but EDL
is only entered on a warm reset, and SDM845's PSCI SYSTEM_RESET is a cold
one.

For the exact restart command "edl", select a warm reset from a reboot
notifier, which runs before the power key driver programs the PMIC's
PS_HOLD reset type from reboot_mode at restart time, and drop PS_HOLD
from the firmware restart handler, which runs right after the SCM
driver's EDL handler. Other restart commands keep the existing
behaviour.

This is local to AGNOS, like the SCM side.

Signed-off-by: Andrei Radulescu <andi.radulescu@gmail.com>
[adeeb: rebase onto the PS_HOLD warm-restart handler, split out of the
 combined SCM and PS_HOLD patch]
Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 drivers/power/reset/msm-poweroff.c | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/reset/msm-poweroff.c b/drivers/power/reset/msm-poweroff.c
index a2b78a32ac..799e73745e 100644
--- a/drivers/power/reset/msm-poweroff.c
+++ b/drivers/power/reset/msm-poweroff.c
@@ -12,10 +12,32 @@
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/reboot.h>
 #include <linux/pm.h>
+#include <linux/string.h>
 
 static void __iomem *msm_ps_hold;
 static bool msm_no_fw_warm_reset;
 
+#define MSM_EDL_REBOOT_PRIORITY	128
+
+static bool msm_is_edl_reboot(const char *cmd)
+{
+	return cmd && !strcmp(cmd, "edl");
+}
+
+static int msm_edl_reboot_notify(struct notifier_block *nb,
+				 unsigned long action, void *data)
+{
+	if (action == SYS_RESTART && msm_is_edl_reboot(data))
+		reboot_mode = REBOOT_WARM;
+
+	return NOTIFY_DONE;
+}
+
+static struct notifier_block msm_edl_reboot_nb = {
+	.notifier_call = msm_edl_reboot_notify,
+	.priority = MSM_EDL_REBOOT_PRIORITY,
+};
+
 static int do_msm_poweroff(struct sys_off_data *data)
 {
 	writel(0, msm_ps_hold);
@@ -26,6 +48,9 @@ static int do_msm_poweroff(struct sys_off_data *data)
 
 static int do_msm_firmware_restart(struct sys_off_data *data)
 {
+	if (msm_is_edl_reboot(data->cmd))
+		return do_msm_poweroff(data);
+
 	/*
 	 * For firmware without a warm reset (no PSCI SYSTEM_RESET2, and a cold
 	 * SYSTEM_RESET), take warm restarts through PS_HOLD, which keeps RAM.
@@ -45,6 +70,11 @@ static int msm_restart_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (IS_ERR(msm_ps_hold))
 		return PTR_ERR(msm_ps_hold);
 
+	ret = devm_register_reboot_notifier(&pdev->dev, &msm_edl_reboot_nb);
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, ret,
+				     "failed to register EDL reboot notifier\n");
+
 	msm_no_fw_warm_reset = of_property_read_bool(pdev->dev.of_node,
 						     "qcom,no-firmware-warm-reset");
 
